  "implementation": [
    "Production grammatical eligibility precedes frequency/similarity; exact contextual native identity is consumed; contradictions abstain with named provenance. Broad native ancestors are not mistaken for exclusions.",
    "Ordinary VERB/ADJ/ADV ambiguity reaches existing grounding; exact whole native source examples retain role/operator/punctuation evidence; no first-sense, flat word-to-prime table or blanket POS selection.",
    "Existing native type-thread _select_by_coherence is the production nominal selector; no alternate cosine/HDC identity resolver.",
    "Public runtime and sentence audits preserve snapshot/benchmark/cohort pins, separate identified/abstained/partial/unavailable/wrong classes, and compute fail-closed checkpoint acceptance with artifact-verified full-scope workload gates.",
    "Native same-synset alias support is tied to an independently unique context definition and existing native type-thread coherence. Production grammatical eligibility must be challenged before an exact He/helium reading can replace pronoun; unrelated chemical mentions retain pronoun.",
    "Exact whole native principal definition clauses can select femur/teacher only on positive complete evidence; partial, questioned, negated or alternative descriptions do not force identity. Strong exact definition witnesses precede weaker derivational support.",
    "Existing native POS and buried-verb repair preserve determined copular nominal heads including degree-adverb modifiers; native AUX is not retyped to content VERB. Genuine buried content verbs still promote.",
    "Existing expression construction preserves spatial preposition relation and temporal nominal anchor. Mixed time/non-time native senses retain explicit unresolved role provenance and a generic relation, not a forced Temporal reading.",
    "Audit chemical/noble-gas positives now require exact helium identity, replacing obsolete expected abstention; insufficient surname context remains a required abstention. This strengthens identity acceptance rather than permitting either result."
  ],
